WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:10.700
Researchers from the Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT) have estimated that the world may need about 1 billion new homes by 2050.
麻省理工学院（MIT）的研究人员估计，到2050年，全世界可能需要约10亿套新住房。

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:22.330
According to a researcher from MIT, if people use wood to make so many homes, an area of forest more than three times the size of the Amazon rainforest may be cut down.
据麻省理工学院的一位研究人员说，如果人们用木材建造这么多住房，被砍伐的森林面积可能是亚马孙雨林的三倍多。

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:28.890
The MIT researchers tried to find other materials to take the place of wood to make house parts.
麻省理工学院的研究人员试图找到其他材料，代替木材来制造房屋构件。

00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:32.450
And they found recycled plastic could play a role.
他们发现，回收塑料可以发挥作用。

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:46.230
The MIT team discovered that recycled plastic mixed with bits of glass could be used as a new material to make trusses—supports put under floors to make sure that the floors can carry the weight of everything on them.
麻省理工学院的团队发现，掺有玻璃碎屑的回收塑料可以用作一种新材料来制造桁架——桁架是放在地板下面的支撑物，用来确保地板能承受上面所有东西的重量。

00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:50.910
The MIT team wanted to know how much weight the trusses could carry.
麻省理工学院的团队想知道这些桁架能承受多少重量。

00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:55.930
In a test, they 3D printed four trusses with the new material.
在一次测试中，他们用这种新材料3D打印了四个桁架。

00:00:56.730 --> 00:01:01.620
Each truss weighed only about 6 kg—lighter than a comparable wooden truss.
每个桁架只重约6千克，比同类的木制桁架轻。

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:07.950
The team put the four trusses under a wooden floor model and slowly added heavy weights on the floor.
研究团队把这四个桁架放在一个木地板模型下面，然后在地板上慢慢加上重物。

00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:17.460
Through the test, the team found the four trusses could sustain objects weighing more than 1,800 kg—about the weight of a car.
通过这次测试，研究团队发现，这四个桁架能承受重量超过1800千克的物体——大约相当于一辆汽车的重量。

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:23.950
This showed trusses made from the new material were strong enough to be used in house building in America.
这表明，用这种新材料制成的桁架足够坚固，可以用于美国的房屋建造。

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:27.220
The finding may benefit house building a lot.
这一发现可能会给房屋建造带来很大好处。

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:33.070
It will be much easier to send house parts made from this new material to different places.
把用这种新材料制成的房屋构件运到不同的地方，会容易得多。

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:39.410
What’s more, the researchers say it is possible to bring down the cost of making house parts.
此外，研究人员说，有可能降低制造房屋构件的成本。

00:01:40.210 --> 00:01:48.920
The researchers hope that one day they can 3D print more house parts with the new material, so that more used plastic can be turned into something useful.
研究人员希望，有一天他们能用这种新材料3D打印更多房屋构件，这样就能把更多废旧塑料变成有用的东西。
